========================================================================
  PART 1: EXACT SEQUENCES FOR G_n
========================================================================

  |V(G_n)| = A000568: 1, 1, 2, 4, 12, 56, 456, 6880, ...
  |E(G_n)| = ?, ?, 1, 5, 30, ?, ...

  n=3: |E|=1, total_weight=6, total_self=12, 2^m*m=24
       total_weight + total_self = 18 = 2^m * m / 2 = 12
  n=4: |E|=5, total_weight=120, total_self=144, 2^m*m=384
       total_weight + total_self = 264 = 2^m * m / 2 = 192
  n=5: |E|=30, total_weight=4240, total_self=1760, 2^m*m=10240
       total_weight + total_self = 6000 = 2^m * m / 2 = 5120

  NOTE: sum_{all i,j} F[i][j] = 2^m * m (double counting).
  So sum_{i<=j} F[i][j] = 2^m * m / 2 (since F symmetric + diagonal).
  Wait: sum_{i,j} F[i][j] = sum_i (size_i * m) = 2^m * m.
  And sum_{i<j} F[i][j] + sum_i F[i][i] = 2^m * m / 2? No.
  Since F[i][j] = F[j][i], sum_{i,j} = 2*sum_{i<j} + sum_i F[i][i].
  So sum_{i<j} F[i][j] = (2^m * m - sum_i F[i][i]) / 2.
  n=3: off-diag weight = (24 - 12)/2 = 6, actual = 6, match = True
  n=4: off-diag weight = (384 - 144)/2 = 120, actual = 120, match = True
  n=5: off-diag weight = (10240 - 1760)/2 = 4240, actual = 4240, match = True

